# Netlify headers (https://docs.netlify.com/routing/headers/)
# When several rules match a URL, Netlify sends all their headers, and the
# same header from two rules is JOINED (comma-separated). So Cache-Control is
# set only in the asset rules below, never in /*.
#
# HTML: no rule needed. Netlify's default for pages is
# "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate" (no-cache: the browser re-checks the
# page on every visit and gets a fresh copy right after each deploy).

# --- Security headers on every response ---------------------------------------
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# --- 1 year, immutable: every file under /assets/ -----------------------------------
# "immutable" means browsers never re-check these files. That is safe because
# every link to them carries a content fingerprint (?v=3f9a2c71) added by
# tools/cache-bust.mjs: change a file → its link changes → browsers fetch it.
# Before every deploy: run npm run prepare-deploy.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
